---
title: Schema explorer, dashboards, and safety
date: '2026-06-16'
tags:
  - added
summary: Source-level schema exploration, dashboard sharing, CSV/chart export, sessions, and a static SQL guard with a PostgreSQL read-only transaction.
---

This source milestone expanded the PostgreSQL prototype from a query page into
a workspace. The schema explorer added table metadata and AI descriptions and
suggestions. Dashboards gained pinned queries, ordering, a public bearer-token
link, and CSV result/chart PNG export paths. Sessions, profile editing, a
connection test route, selectable AI-provider configuration, and a health route
were also added.

A static SQL guard and PostgreSQL `READ ONLY` transaction restrict execution;
they do not guarantee query safety or answer accuracy. Anyone holding a shared
dashboard token can rerun its pinned queries without signing in, and results
can change. The prototype needs bounded-result, connection-transport, and
share-permission review before use with sensitive data.

The former paired images showed an older marketing landing, not a captured
query or dashboard workflow. They visibly advertised a waitlist, MySQL support,
performance and success metrics without verification, and a false claim that
data never leaves the database. Those stills are withdrawn. Real paired
light/dark product captures and narrated release films remain to be made.
